# Fortran build artifacts. gfortran writes a .mod into the CURRENT WORKING
# DIRECTORY for every `module` it compiles — including under
# `gfortran -fsyntax-only`, which is how 32 of them from numpy's f2py test
# corpus ended up committed at the repo root. They are regenerated by every
# build and belong to no source tree.
*.mod
*.smod
*.o
